  "administrativeMessages": [
    {
      "purpose": "entry",
      "id": "1184869680033321001",
      "channelId": "1184864166142558349",
      "createdAt": "2023-12-14T14:49:05.534000+00:00",
      "editedAt": "2025-03-04T15:23:56.375000+00:00",
      "pinned": false,
      "author": {
        "id": "681333902740160598",
        "username": "emsenn",
        "kind": "administrator"
      },
      "applicationId": null,
      "webhookId": null,
      "flags": 0,
      "content": "***Turntide Islands***\n\n**Turntide Islands** is a virtual space focused on responding, not reacting, to climate weirding.\n\nPeople gather here to share knowledge and build practices and communities that are grounded in an honest acceptance of the compound crises that affect us, from climate weirding to catabolic collapse.\n\nMembers are expected to engage with care and curiosity, treating others with respect. No spam, scams, or doxxing. Violation of Discord's Terms of Service will result in a mute.\n\nTurntide Islands exists as a decentralized autonomous organization (DAO) using polycentric participatory consensus. Proposals are discussed openly, quorum-based votes determine outcomes, and all governance actions are permanently recorded on-chain for accountability. Each topical area follows the same discussion → quorum vote → recorded decision structure, allowing decentralized yet organized decision-making across the community. (In the future, participation may be recognized with tokens that influence governance weight, ensuring active contributors have a meaningful say.)\n\nTurntide Islands is administrated by emsenn, who documents and implements all governance decisions. (In the future, an automation may handle these technical actions.)\n\nTo join Turntide Islands, use the invite link to enter the Discord server and click the 🏝️ emoji below the welcome message. Once verified, you can explore and join topical communities by selecting the corresponding emojis.",
      "contentWithheld": false,
